   358                          ;; RESTART and GRAB:
   359                          ;;
   360                          ;; GRAB checks that the caller passed enough arguments onto the stack. If not,
   361                          ;; it creates a closure, stores all the available arguments in it, points the
   362                          ;; closure code to the instruction just before GRAB (which is assumed to be a
   363                          ;; RESTART), then returns to the caller, as if executing a RETURN instruction.
   364                          ;; When the new closure is called, RESTART will push the arguments onto the
   365                          ;; stack again and fallthrough GRAB.
